1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:06,570
Part three asks what DexPilot demonstrated in its twenty nineteen physical-robot study.
下篇要问的是：DexPilot在2019年的研究中，究竟在真实机器人上证明了什么。

2
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:11,550
The evaluation covers fifteen tasks performed by two trained human pilots.
评估包含15项任务，由两名训练过的操作者完成。

3
00:00:11,930 --> 00:00:17,670
It tests grasping, releasing, pushing, sliding, and changing finger contacts during manipulation.
它测试抓取、释放、推、滑，以及操作过程中切换手指接触。

4
00:00:18,230 --> 00:00:23,050
The human supplies task judgment, decisions, and corrections throughout teleoperation.
整个遥操作过程中，人持续判断任务进展，作出决策和修正。

5
00:00:23,590 --> 00:00:28,110
These are teleoperated results, without demonstrated autonomous task policies.
这些是人操控机器人的结果；论文没有展示完成这些任务的自主策略。

6
00:00:28,799 --> 00:00:33,999
Three pick-and-place tasks use a foam brick, a Pringles can, and a Spam box.
三项抓放任务分别使用泡沫砖、品客薯片罐和午餐肉盒。

7
00:00:34,419 --> 00:00:39,799
Three stacking tasks use large, medium, and small blocks, each requiring a three-block tower.
三项堆叠任务分别使用大、中、小方块，都要叠起三块。

8
00:00:40,319 --> 00:00:45,759
Other tasks include pouring beads, opening a jar, rotating a brick, and opening a container.
其余任务包括倒珠子、开罐、转动砖块和打开容器。

9
00:00:46,259 --> 00:00:52,919
They also include cup insertion, retrieving tea, sliding a card, extracting money, and flipping a box.
还包括套杯、取茶包、滑卡片、取纸币和翻盒子。

10
00:00:53,459 --> 00:00:57,639
These are fifteen distinct variants, not fifteen repetitions of one grasp.
这15项来自不同任务变体，而不是同一种抓握重复15次。

11
00:00:58,206 --> 00:01:02,866
Pilots warm up with three to five nonconsecutive attempts per task.
正式测试每项任务前，操作者先做3到5次非连续热身尝试。

12
00:01:03,186 --> 00:01:08,506
Each then performs five consecutive trials, reducing selection of favorable attempts.
之后每位操作者连续完成5次测试，以减少挑选有利试次的问题。

13
00:01:08,926 --> 00:01:12,486
An object falling outside the workspace counts as a failed trial.
物体掉出工作空间，记为失败。

14
00:01:12,886 --> 00:01:17,566
A dropped object can sometimes be recovered inside the workspace to complete the task.
如果物体仍在工作空间内，有时可以重新捡起，最终完成任务。

15
00:01:18,166 --> 00:01:23,346
Success means completing this protocol, not executing every intermediate action without mistakes.
因此，成功表示按这一协议完成任务，并不意味着每个中间动作都毫无失误。

16
00:01:24,011 --> 00:01:28,351
For one pilot on one task, the denominator is only five attempts.
对某位操作者的某项任务，分母只有5次尝试。

17
00:01:28,651 --> 00:01:33,511
One additional failure changes the reported success rate by twenty percentage points.
多一次失败，就会让报告成功率变化20个百分点。

18
00:01:33,971 --> 00:01:39,351
Counting the complete table gives one hundred and forty-one successes in one hundred and fifty attempts.
全表共150次尝试；根据记录的失败项重算，共141次成功。

19
00:01:39,731 --> 00:01:45,251
This pooled total is our calculation; combining tasks hides important difficulty differences.
这个合计是我们计算的，而把不同任务混在一起会掩盖重要的难度差异。

20
00:01:45,551 --> 00:01:51,051
The comparison is between teleoperators, without a timed direct-human manipulation baseline.
这里比较的是两名遥操作者；论文没有计时的真人直接操作基线。

21
00:01:51,651 --> 00:01:56,271
For foam-brick pick and place, both pilots succeed in all five trials.
泡沫砖抓放中，两名操作者都5次全部成功。

22
00:01:56,771 --> 00:02:01,051
The appendix reports mean completion times of sixteen and nineteen seconds.
附录报告的平均完成时间分别为16秒和19秒。

23
00:02:01,431 --> 00:02:07,551
For card sliding, both again succeed five times, but the means are thirty-two and sixteen seconds.
滑卡片任务中，两人也都成功5次，但均值分别为32秒和16秒。

24
00:02:08,151 --> 00:02:13,191
These are rounded task means, not reaction times or isolated controller timings.
这些是按操作者统计并取整的任务均值，不是人的反应时间，也不是单独控制器耗时。

25
00:02:13,611 --> 00:02:16,491
The measured system includes the person and their strategy.
这些差异说明，被测系统包括操作者本人及其策略。

26
00:02:17,183 --> 00:02:22,763
The block side lengths are six point three, three point eight, and two point three centimeters.
方块边长分别为6.3、3.8和2.3厘米。

27
00:02:23,403 --> 00:02:29,763
For the smallest blocks, pilot one succeeds four times out of five, while pilot two succeeds five times.
最小方块任务中，操作者一5次成功4次，操作者二5次全部成功。

28
00:02:30,203 --> 00:02:35,063
Their reported completion-time means are two hundred and ninety seconds and ninety-one seconds.
报告的平均完成时间分别为290秒和91秒。

29
00:02:35,523 --> 00:02:39,563
The appendix confirms that the failed attempt is excluded from the first mean.
根据附录逐次数据可确认，操作者一的均值统计中排除了失败试次。

30
00:02:39,883 --> 00:02:45,743
Read successful-only times beside success counts, especially when performance varies this much.
因此，尤其当表现差异很大时，只对成功试次计算的时间必须和成功次数一起读。

31
00:02:46,268 --> 00:02:52,628
The wallet task requires opening the wallet and pulling out paper money, while retaining useful contact.
钱包任务要求打开钱包，再抽出纸币，同时维持有效接触。

32
00:02:52,848 --> 00:02:58,908
Both pilots complete all five trials, with reported means of one hundred and five and two hundred and twelve seconds.
两人都完成5次，报告均值分别为105秒和212秒。

33
00:02:59,068 --> 00:03:05,508
The container task requires opening a plastic container, extracting a cardboard box, and opening that box.
容器任务需要打开塑料容器，取出纸盒，再打开纸盒。

34
00:03:05,908 --> 00:03:11,613
Both pilots again succeed five times, with means of three hundred and fifty-eight and two hundred and twenty-eight seconds.
两人同样5次全部成功，均值分别为358秒和228秒。

35
00:03:11,628 --> 00:03:17,208
These sequences establish feasible teleoperated solutions, alongside their long durations.
这些序列证明了遥操作解的可行性，而较长耗时同样是结果的一部分。

36
00:03:17,737 --> 00:03:22,857
Brick gaiting asks the robot to rotate a grasped brick by one hundred and eighty degrees.
砖块换指任务要求机器人把握住的砖块旋转180度。

37
00:03:23,437 --> 00:03:29,977
Both pilots succeed in three of five trials, with successful-trial means of fifty-eight and thirty-six seconds.
两人都是5次成功3次，成功试次均值分别为58秒和36秒。

38
00:03:30,677 --> 00:03:36,397
Figure sixteen separately illustrates seven middle-finger contacts over a forty-second rotation sequence.
图16另外展示了一段40秒旋转序列，其中中指发生7次接触。

39
00:03:36,957 --> 00:03:40,997
The thumb and ring finger remain pinched while the middle finger changes contact.
拇指和无名指保持捏持，中指则切换接触。

40
00:03:41,437 --> 00:03:46,517
The tactile trace explains one behavior; the table measures full-task reliability.
触觉曲线解释一次行为；五次试验的表格衡量完整任务成功得有多稳定。

41
00:03:47,302 --> 00:03:56,102
Projection helps compensate for uncertain fingertip geometry, but the paper reports interference with finger gaiting and small-object release.
投影有助于补偿不确定的指尖几何，但论文报告它会干扰换指和小物体释放。

42
00:03:56,622 --> 00:04:01,182
Figure eighteen shows the resulting difficulty of releasing small objects cleanly.
图18展示了由此带来的小物体干净释放困难。

43
00:04:01,482 --> 00:04:04,522
The authors say projection can be turned off when desired.
作者表示，可以按需要关闭投影。

44
00:04:04,822 --> 00:04:10,702
However, the task table does not document a controlled projection-on versus projection-off experiment.
不过，任务表没有记录受控的开启与关闭投影对照实验。

45
00:04:11,102 --> 00:04:16,662
We can explain this tradeoff, but cannot quantify its causal contribution to success or failure.
我们可以解释机制与报告的权衡，却不能给它分配成功或失败的定量因果贡献。

46
00:04:17,260 --> 00:04:22,980
The pilot observation volume measures eighty by fifty-five by thirty-eight centimeters.
操作者的观测空间为80乘55乘38厘米。

47
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:29,620
Hand self-occlusion and tracking robustness across different hand sizes and shapes remain concerns.
手部自遮挡，以及不同手型和尺寸下的跟踪鲁棒性，仍然是问题。

48
00:04:30,140 --> 00:04:35,200
The pilot sees the nearby robot but receives no tactile feedback from its fingertips.
操作者可以观察附近的机器人，却收不到机器人指尖的触觉反馈。

49
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:41,545
Recording tactile signals does not provide human sensation or automatic grasp-force regulation.
因此，记录了触觉信号，并不意味着人能感到接触，或控制器已经自动调节抓握力。

50
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:47,300
Approximately one-second latency and motion-generator responsiveness also need improvement.
论文还把约1秒延迟和运动生成器响应速度列为需要改进的限制。

51
00:04:47,991 --> 00:04:53,511
The authors also attempt NIST-board peg insertion, outside the fifteen-task benchmark.
作者还尝试了NIST任务板上的紧配合插接，它不属于15项基准任务表。

52
00:04:53,831 --> 00:04:59,031
Figure seventeen shows one successful insertion with a zero point one millimeter hole clearance.
图17展示了一次成功插入，孔隙间隙为0.1毫米。

53
00:04:59,471 --> 00:05:07,831
But the text describes these results as mostly unsatisfactory, with success rates typically within ten percent under specific initial placements.
但正文称整体结果大多不理想，在特定初始摆放条件下，成功率通常不超过10%。

54
00:05:08,351 --> 00:05:12,976
The trial count is unreported, preventing conversion into a precise success fraction.
论文没有提供对应试次总数，因此不能把它改写成精确分数。

55
00:05:12,991 --> 00:05:18,291
One demonstration supports possibility; low reliability limits the broader claim.
一次有说服力的演示支持可行性，而报告的低可靠性限制了更广泛的结论。

56
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:25,820
DexPilot records robot-side signals including ninety-two tactile channels, joint states, and torque commands.
DexPilot记录机器人侧信号，包括92路触觉、关节状态和力矩指令。

57
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:31,560
These demonstrations contain actual robot interactions, because the robot performs the actions.
动作直接发生在机器人上，因此示范包含了机器人的真实物理交互。

58
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:37,160
Recoveries and changing contacts may provide useful learning material, as the authors propose.
正如作者提出的，失败恢复与接触变化可能提供有用的学习素材。

59
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:42,080
Training and evaluating autonomous policies from these data is explicitly future work.
但在这里，用这些数据训练并评估自主任务策略，被明确列为未来工作。

60
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:48,080
The contribution enables teleoperation and data collection, without demonstrated autonomous mastery.
证据支持的贡献是遥操作与数据采集基础，而不是自主掌握整套任务。

61
00:05:48,626 --> 00:05:55,746
A useful conceptual contrast is TeleDexter, which learns a controller to follow both hand and object targets.
一个有用的概念对照是TeleDexter，它学习同时跟踪手与物体目标的控制器。

62
00:05:56,246 --> 00:06:03,726
DexPilot instead turns observed bare-hand motion into geometric finger commands and palm motion, with the pilot closing the task loop.
DexPilot则把观测到的裸手动作转为手指几何指令与手掌运动，由操作者闭合任务回路。

63
00:06:04,106 --> 00:06:09,026
Different hardware, tasks, and protocols prevent a direct numerical ranking from these papers.
硬件、任务与协议不同，不能从这两篇论文直接作数值排名。

64
00:06:09,546 --> 00:06:16,691
This twenty nineteen system demonstrates repeated physical teleoperation across diverse tasks, with documented limitations.
对这个2019年的系统，最有力的证据是多样任务中的重复实物遥操作，以及明确记录的限制。

65
00:06:16,706 --> 00:06:26,146
Its enduring lesson is to preserve useful fingertip relationships, then evaluate the complete human-robot interaction rather than a convincing hand pose alone.
它留下的方法启示是：保留有用的指尖关系，再评估完整的人机交互，而不只看手型是否逼真。
